{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/6308-pdf-accessibility-questions-and-concerns","id":6308,"title":"PDF Accessibility Questions and Concerns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-08T13:54:19-08:00","id":6308,"title":"PDF Accessibility Questions and Concerns","content":"Hi All,<br /> <br /> I am a long time player of White-Wolf games (since about 1999), with a permanent visual disability. The move to PDF books in the early 2000s was a great boon to me and dramatically improved how I play and run games. Once PDFs were released in OEF (original electronic format) rather than scanned documents, this functionality only improved. In order to read these books I use various screen readers (JAWS for Windows at the current time, but transitioning to NVDA and Voiceover).<br /> <br /> Recently this functionality has begone to slip. The last two downloads I made (Reap the Whirlwind and GMC Rules Update) were totally unreadable. My wife has had to OCR the GMC Update and copy it into a word format for me to read.<br /> <br /> Although my collection is not comprehensive, after the move to OEF, I have only faced this difficulty with the Exalted 2nd Edition Core. I am curious if coding of these products has changed, or if there is something that I am missing. I love WW games and want to continue playing them, but the loss of accessibility is frustrating to a great degree.<br /> <br /> Appologies for the long first post. Thanks to anyone who can help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/734-zombie_eyes","name":"Zombie_Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}